Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"68.197.9.143","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5d960ded79d3a451ccb7627c7b57456c","RawContent":"Hello. I&#039;m new to tala talk. I posted a question but got one reply to search the forums. \n\nI&#039;m planning a DW for May, 2015. \n\nI&#039;ve met w a travel agent and have been reading forums. \n\nI can&#039;t find anything on Westin Lagunamar Cancun for wedding experiences. How was it ? Any advise?\n\nMpt\n\n\n\nSent from my iPad using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1879343,"PostDate":1417298223,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Hello. I'm new to tala talk. I posted a question but got one reply to search the forums. <br>\nI'm planning a DW for May, 2015. <br>\nI've met w a travel agent and have been reading forums. <br>\nI can't find anything on Westin Lagunamar Cancun for wedding experiences. How was it ? Any advise?<br>\nMpt<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPad using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mptorres78@gmail.com","IpAddress":"68.197.9.143","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1417121004,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"mtorres2002","Id":281260,"Name":"mtorres2002","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8d042105575eda7c76e5451ee2ba86a2","RawContent":"[quote name=\"mtorres2002\" post=\"1879343\" timestamp=\"1417327023\"]\nHello. I&#039;m new to tala talk. I posted a question but got one reply to search the forums.\nI&#039;m planning a DW for May, 2015.\nI&#039;ve met w a travel agent and have been reading forums.\nI can&#039;t find anything on Westin Lagunamar Cancun for wedding experiences. How was it ? Any advise?\nMpt\n\n\nSent from my iPad using Tapatalk[\/quote]\nWelcome,\nI did a quick search on the Westin resort you mentioned above and noone has reviewed this resort. It doesn&#039;t seem many people have even posted about it - so not sure how to help you there.\nOtherwise I agree about searching the resorts you are considering because there are threads on them and you will learn sooooo much from past brides.   Also the board here in general will give you a lot of ideas for your wedding.\n\nCongrats!","Attachments":[],"Id":1879345,"PostDate":1417302717,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>mtorres2002, on 29 November 2014 - 09:57 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Hello. I'm new to tala talk. I posted a question but got one reply to search the forums.<br>\nI'm planning a DW for May, 2015.<br>\nI've met w a travel agent and have been reading forums.<br>\nI can't find anything on Westin Lagunamar Cancun for wedding experiences. How was it ? Any advise?<br>\nMpt<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPad using Tapatalk<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Welcome,<\/p>\n<p>I did a quick search on the Westin resort you mentioned above and noone has reviewed this resort. It doesn't seem many people have even posted about it - so not sure how to help you there.<\/p>\n<p>Otherwise I agree about searching the resorts you are considering because there are threads on them and you will learn sooooo much from past brides. \u00a0 Also the board here in general will give you a lot of ideas for your wedding.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Congrats!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>43 guests, plus bride and groom \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399399802,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"201.138.28.241","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c502fdacef23bb8f84c7ec353eb5ec00","RawContent":"[quote name=\"mtorres2002\" post=\"1879343\" timestamp=\"1417327023\"]\nHello. I&#039;m new to tala talk. I posted a question but got one reply to search the forums.\nI&#039;m planning a DW for May, 2015.\nI&#039;ve met w a travel agent and have been reading forums.\nI can&#039;t find anything on Westin Lagunamar Cancun for wedding experiences. How was it ? Any advise?\nMpt\n\n\nSent from my iPad using Tapatalk[\/quote] Hi @[member=\"mtorres2002\"]\n \nCongratulations on your engagement!! \nI would like to welcome you to the best destination wedding site, where you will find lots of information regarding wedding venue locations, details,etc... \nIf you&#039;d like to you can visit our website [url=\"http:\/\/www.adventureweddingsvallarta.com\/\"]www.adventureweddingsvallarta.com[\/url] and check out our wedding packages, we have a beautiful private beach called Las Caletas in Puerto Vallarta, Mexico, where we make the magic happen with an amazing view and an awesome setting for your ceremony. \nIf you want to speak with a sales agent for further assistance feel free to contact us at toll free 1.866.731.8152 or e-mail us to [email=\"info@adventureweddingsvallarta.com\"]info@adventureweddingsvallarta.com[\/email]\n \n \nBest regards,\n \n \nAdventure Weddings.","Attachments":[],"Id":1879411,"PostDate":1417430434,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>mtorres2002, on 29 November 2014 - 09:57 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<p>Hello. I'm new to tala talk. I posted a question but got one reply to search the forums.<br>\nI'm planning a DW for May, 2015.<br>\nI've met w a travel agent and have been reading forums.<br>\nI can't find anything on Westin Lagunamar Cancun for wedding experiences. How was it ? Any advise?<br>\nMpt<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPad using Tapatalk<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0Hi @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281260\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281260-mtorres2002\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">mtorres2002<\/span><\/a><br>\n\u00a0<br>\nCongratulations on your engagement!!\u00a0<br>\nI would like to welcome you to the best destination wedding site, where you will find lots of information regarding wedding venue locations, details,etc...\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\nIf you'd like to\u00a0you\u00a0can\u00a0visit our website <a href='http:\/\/www.adventureweddingsvallarta.com\/' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>www.adventureweddingsvallarta.com<\/a> and check out our wedding packages, we have a beautiful private beach called Las Caletas in Puerto Vallarta, Mexico, where we make the magic happen with an amazing view and an\u00a0awesome setting for your ceremony.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\nIf you want to speak with a sales agent for further assistance feel free to contact us at toll free 1.866.731.8152 or e-mail us to <a href='mailto:info@adventureweddingsvallarta.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>info@adventureweddingsvallarta.com<\/a><br>\n\u00a0<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nBest regards,<br>\n\u00a0<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nAdventure Weddings.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"dennise@adventureweddingsvallarta.com","IpAddress":"187.146.166.254","GroupId":49,"GroupName":"Insiders","JoinDate":1343030003,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-258213.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":100,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"LasCaletas","Id":258213,"Name":"LasCaletas","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"71.194.13.101","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"06e559679a5c4c66f2effcfcfdb45918","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;New Bride here! &amp;nbsp;Well we have been engaged for almost a year, but the wedding planning is still just starting....again. &amp;nbsp;I originally wanted a destination wedding but after discussing it with my parents (who are paying) it changed to a Chicago wedding, until they realized it would be at least $20,000 with a miserable daughter\/bride planning it all! So back to the drawing board.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately I think I lost all my excitement for the wedding. &amp;nbsp;I am having a hard time keeping track of different resorts and pricing and am getting depressed by the thought of my wedding, which, of course makes me sadder! AH!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We want to have it on the beach. &amp;nbsp;Mexico-Mayan Riviera (would like to see ruins) or Hawaii. &amp;nbsp;About 20-30 people. &amp;nbsp;Beautiful? &amp;nbsp;Easiest? &amp;nbsp;Affordable? &amp;nbsp;Am I crazy? I need some help. &amp;nbsp;I would like the wedding ceremony\/reception\/my parents flights\/ my parents hotel stay all for under $10,000. &amp;nbsp;Is that possible???? &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Any responses would be appreciated. &amp;nbsp;We haven&#039;t set a date, waiting to find the resort! &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1879451,"PostDate":1417508323,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>New Bride here! \u00a0Well we have been engaged for almost a year, but the wedding planning is still just starting....again. \u00a0I originally wanted a destination wedding but after discussing it with my parents (who are paying) it changed to a Chicago wedding, until they realized it would be at least $20,000 with a miserable daughter\/bride planning it all! So back to the drawing board.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Unfortunately I think I lost all my excitement for the wedding. \u00a0I am having a hard time keeping track of different resorts and pricing and am getting depressed by the thought of my wedding, which, of course makes me sadder! AH!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We want to have it on the beach. \u00a0Mexico-Mayan Riviera (would like to see ruins) or Hawaii. \u00a0About 20-30 people. \u00a0Beautiful? \u00a0Easiest? \u00a0Affordable? \u00a0Am I crazy? I need some help. \u00a0I would like the wedding ceremony\/reception\/my parents flights\/ my parents hotel stay all for under $10,000. \u00a0Is that possible???? \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Any responses would be appreciated. \u00a0We haven't set a date, waiting to find the resort! \u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"goldammerpayne@gmail.com","IpAddress":"71.194.13.101","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1416924099,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"goldammerpayne","Id":281246,"Name":"goldammerpayne","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"159.53.46.141","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"05f1cb6e52ded87e48423b6edd3bbfc1","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hi @goldammarpayne. I&#039;m in Chicago, too, and $20k for a wedding here would be a total STEAL. My friends who got married in the city paid upwards of $50k, which to me is just absolutely insane. I think it is completely possible to do what you describe for 20-30 people for $10,000! We are expecting probably 50 people for our wedding in Jamaica and our budget is $15,000, including our travel, my dress, photography, etc. While we really wanted to get married when the weather is horrible in Chicago, prices were much more expensive January through Easter, so I would avoid those months to save money if you can.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The good thing is most all inclusive resorts make it really easy on you with on-site planners who work with you on all the details. (And this site will help you get a lot of questions answered.) You can make it as simple or complicated as you want. We aren&#039;t doing a bridal party and we&#039;re bringing pretty minimal decorations to keep it easy.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I&#039;ve been to a few resorts in Mexico. We really liked RIU Palace Riviera Maya and my sister got married at Catalonia Riviera Maya, which was a very affordable option. But definitely browse around the forums here and you&#039;ll get some great ideas. Have you reached out to a travel agent yet? They can definitely help you narrow down your options!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Also, I completely empathize with NOT being excited about your wedding. I actually had a meltdown just this weekend and tried to convince my fiance that we should skip it all and just elope. (He laughed at me! Ha.) We&#039;ve had a series of crappy things happen since we got engaged last December and I guess that is probably why, and I&#039;m just hoping as we get closer to the date I&#039;ll get more excited. I better!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1879459,"PostDate":1417512915,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hi @goldammarpayne. I'm in Chicago, too, and $20k for a wedding here would be a total STEAL. My friends who got married in the city paid upwards of $50k, which to me is just absolutely insane. I think it is completely possible to do what you describe for 20-30 people for $10,000! We are expecting probably 50 people for our wedding in Jamaica and our budget is $15,000, including our travel, my dress, photography, etc. While we really wanted to get married when the weather is horrible in Chicago, prices were much more expensive January through Easter, so I would avoid those months to save money if you can.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The good thing is most all inclusive resorts make it really easy on you with on-site planners who work with you on all the details. (And this site will help you get a lot of questions answered.) You can make it as simple or complicated as you want. We aren't doing a bridal party and we're bringing pretty minimal decorations to keep it easy.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I've been to a few resorts in Mexico. We really liked RIU Palace Riviera Maya and my sister got married at Catalonia Riviera Maya, which was a very affordable option. But definitely browse around the forums here and you'll get some great ideas. Have you reached out to a travel agent yet? They can definitely help you narrow down your options!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Also, I completely empathize with NOT being excited about your wedding. I actually had a meltdown just this weekend and tried to convince my fiance that we should skip it all and just elope. (He laughed at me! Ha.) We've had a series of crappy things happen since we got engaged last December and I guess that is probably why, and I'm just hoping as we get closer to the date I'll get more excited. I better!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rebecca.shaffer@gmail.com","IpAddress":"159.53.174.144","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1403087287,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"beckys98","Id":278581,"Name":"beckys98","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"71.194.13.101","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"97a39a5a299e3e738e49c188d7365e28","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Thank you Becky! &amp;nbsp;I will check out Catalonia for sure! &amp;nbsp;This forum is a godsend, and although I have been a lurker taking the plunge into posting will hopefully help me get organized :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Yes, the $20k chicago wedding was for a backyard wedding, needless to say it was more than what I wanted to spend for one day of incredible stress! The $4,700 tent quote was what killed it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I hope you get more excited too!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Does anyone have a travel agent they would recommend? &amp;nbsp;I&#039;ll keep looking!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1879475,"PostDate":1417517648,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Thank you Becky! \u00a0I will check out Catalonia for sure! \u00a0This forum is a godsend, and although I have been a lurker taking the plunge into posting will hopefully help me get organized <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Yes, the $20k chicago wedding was for a backyard wedding, needless to say it was more than what I wanted to spend for one day of incredible stress! The $4,700 tent quote was what killed it.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I hope you get more excited too!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Does anyone have a travel agent they would recommend? \u00a0I'll keep looking!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"goldammerpayne@gmail.com","IpAddress":"71.194.13.101","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1416924099,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"goldammerpayne","Id":281246,"Name":"goldammerpayne","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"201.138.11.30","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"25ac938b84a61d2d5780fe755fc91029","RawContent":"[quote name=\"goldammerpayne\" post=\"1879475\" timestamp=\"1417546448\"]\nThank you Becky!  I will check out Catalonia for sure!  This forum is a godsend, and although I have been a lurker taking the plunge into posting will hopefully help me get organized :)\n\nYes, the $20k chicago wedding was for a backyard wedding, needless to say it was more than what I wanted to spend for one day of incredible stress! The $4,700 tent quote was what killed it. \n\nI hope you get more excited too!!\n\nDoes anyone have a travel agent they would recommend?  I&#039;ll keep looking![\/quote]\nHello! @[member=\"goldammerpayne\"]\n :)\n\nCongratulations on your engagement!! :wub:\n\nI would like to welcome you to the best destination wedding site, where you will find lots of information regarding wedding venue locations, details,etc...\n\nIf you&#039;d like to you can visit our website [url=\"http:\/\/www.adventureweddingsvallarta.com\/\"]www.adventureweddingsvallarta.com[\/url] and check out our wedding packages, we have a beautiful private beach called Las Caletas in Puerto Vallarta, Mexico, where we make the magic happen with an amazing view and an awesome setting for your ceremony.\n\nIf you want to speak with a sales agent for further assistance feel free to contact us at toll free 1.866.731.8152 or e-mail us to [email=\"info@adventureweddingsvallarta.com\"]info@adventureweddingsvallarta.com[\/email]\n\n\nBest regards,\nAdventure weddings team!","Attachments":[],"Id":1879498,"PostDate":1417526135,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>goldammerpayne, on 02 December 2014 - 10:54 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>Thank you Becky! \u00a0I will check out Catalonia for sure! \u00a0This forum is a godsend, and although I have been a lurker taking the plunge into posting will hopefully help me get organized <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Yes, the $20k chicago wedding was for a backyard wedding, needless to say it was more than what I wanted to spend for one day of incredible stress! The $4,700 tent quote was what killed it.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I hope you get more excited too!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Does anyone have a travel agent they would recommend? \u00a0I'll keep looking!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Hello! @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281246\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281246-goldammerpayne\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">goldammerpayne<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p> <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Congratulations on your engagement!! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/wub.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':wub:' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I would like to welcome you to the best destination wedding site, where you will find lots of information regarding wedding venue locations, details,etc...<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>If you'd like to\u00a0you\u00a0can\u00a0visit our website <a href='http:\/\/www.adventureweddingsvallarta.com\/' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>www.adventureweddingsvallarta.com<\/a> and check out our wedding packages, we have a beautiful private beach called Las Caletas in Puerto Vallarta, Mexico, where we make the magic happen with an amazing view and an\u00a0awesome setting for your ceremony.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>If you want to speak with a sales agent for further assistance feel free to contact us at toll free 1.866.731.8152 or e-mail us to <a href='mailto:info@adventureweddingsvallarta.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>info@adventureweddingsvallarta.com<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Best regards,<\/p>\n<p>Adventure weddings team!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"dennise@adventureweddingsvallarta.com","IpAddress":"187.146.166.254","GroupId":49,"GroupName":"Insiders","JoinDate":1343030003,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-258213.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":100,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"LasCaletas","Id":258213,"Name":"LasCaletas","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"135.23.79.200","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5fb072cfa44b9bedd63cf164a488af77","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Congratulations and happy planning :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1880633,"PostDate":1418835087,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Congratulations and happy planning <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"vsschick@gmail.com","IpAddress":"162.208.80.15","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1404455510,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"vsschick1234","Id":278832,"Name":"vsschick1234","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"64.53.250.35","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"6d260ca3f40743a0d7751496ae17d585","RawContent":"[quote name=\"goldammerpayne\" post=\"1879451\" timestamp=\"1417537123\"]\nNew Bride here!  Well we have been engaged for almost a year, but the wedding planning is still just starting....again.  I originally wanted a destination wedding but after discussing it with my parents (who are paying) it changed to a Chicago wedding, until they realized it would be at least $20,000 with a miserable daughter\/bride planning it all! So back to the drawing board.\n\nUnfortunately I think I lost all my excitement for the wedding.  I am having a hard time keeping track of different resorts and pricing and am getting depressed by the thought of my wedding, which, of course makes me sadder! AH!\n\nWe want to have it on the beach.  Mexico-Mayan Riviera (would like to see ruins) or Hawaii.  About 20-30 people.  Beautiful?  Easiest?  Affordable?  Am I crazy? I need some help.  I would like the wedding ceremony\/reception\/my parents flights\/ my parents hotel stay all for under $10,000.  Is that possible????  \n\nAny responses would be appreciated.  We haven&#039;t set a date, waiting to find the resort![\/quote]\nI think it&#039;s hard to go wrong with the Riviera Maya, but I might be biased since that&#039;s where mine is :)  All of our guests have been SHOCKED at how affordable it is, especially those who haven&#039;t been on a \"tropical\" vacation before, and still lots of history and activities, and travel (from Cleveland, at least) has always been a piece of cake.  My resort is the Now Jade--beautiful, affordable, and AWESOME food (we&#039;ve visited several times).  I&#039;d definitely recommend it!","Attachments":[],"Id":1880740,"PostDate":1418881382,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>goldammerpayne, on 02 December 2014 - 08:18 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>New Bride here! \u00a0Well we have been engaged for almost a year, but the wedding planning is still just starting....again. \u00a0I originally wanted a destination wedding but after discussing it with my parents (who are paying) it changed to a Chicago wedding, until they realized it would be at least $20,000 with a miserable daughter\/bride planning it all! So back to the drawing board.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Unfortunately I think I lost all my excitement for the wedding. \u00a0I am having a hard time keeping track of different resorts and pricing and am getting depressed by the thought of my wedding, which, of course makes me sadder! AH!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We want to have it on the beach. \u00a0Mexico-Mayan Riviera (would like to see ruins) or Hawaii. \u00a0About 20-30 people. \u00a0Beautiful? \u00a0Easiest? \u00a0Affordable? \u00a0Am I crazy? I need some help. \u00a0I would like the wedding ceremony\/reception\/my parents flights\/ my parents hotel stay all for under $10,000. \u00a0Is that possible???? \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Any responses would be appreciated. \u00a0We haven't set a date, waiting to find the resort! \u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I think it's hard to go wrong with the Riviera Maya, but I might be biased since that's where mine is <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \u00a0All of our guests have been SHOCKED at how affordable it is, especially those who haven't been on a \"tropical\" vacation before, and still lots of history and activities, and travel (from Cleveland, at least) has always been a piece of cake. \u00a0My resort is the Now Jade--beautiful, affordable, and AWESOME food (we've visited several times). \u00a0I'd definitely recommend it!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rachelia160@aim.com","IpAddress":"66.61.104.237","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1388703097,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-275855.jpg?_r=1414697242","PhotoWidth":185,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"rachelia160","Id":275855,"Name":"rachelia160","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":true,"CanDelete":true,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78298,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"85f5e36e4676d211a39251b749ab79fb","RawContent":"[quote name=\"goldammerpayne\" post=\"1879451\" timestamp=\"1417537123\"]\nNew Bride here!  Well we have been engaged for almost a year, but the wedding planning is still just starting....again.  I originally wanted a destination wedding but after discussing it with my parents (who are paying) it changed to a Chicago wedding, until they realized it would be at least $20,000 with a miserable daughter\/bride planning it all! So back to the drawing board.\n\nUnfortunately I think I lost all my excitement for the wedding.  I am having a hard time keeping track of different resorts and pricing and am getting depressed by the thought of my wedding, which, of course makes me sadder! AH!\n\nWe want to have it on the beach.  Mexico-Mayan Riviera (would like to see ruins) or Hawaii.  About 20-30 people.  Beautiful?  Easiest?  Affordable?  Am I crazy? I need some help.  I would like the wedding ceremony\/reception\/my parents flights\/ my parents hotel stay all for under $10,000.  Is that possible????  \n\nAny responses would be appreciated.  We haven&#039;t set a date, waiting to find the resort![\/quote]Hello!\nI&#039;m marrying at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya and my wedding for 46 on the private beach and reception in the private palapa is about $5200. \n\nAfter our booking bonuses with the airline our package for 7 nights (flight\/hotel\/transfers\/tax) for 2 adults and 2 kids was $3100 (was $5100) so with that said I think $10,000 is very doable. \n\nIf you want more info on the resort let me know. Good luck.    \n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1880789,"PostDate":1418928925,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>goldammerpayne, on 02 December 2014 - 08:18 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>New Bride here!  Well we have been engaged for almost a year, but the wedding planning is still just starting....again.  I originally wanted a destination wedding but after discussing it with my parents (who are paying) it changed to a Chicago wedding, until they realized it would be at least $20,000 with a miserable daughter\/bride planning it all! So back to the drawing board.<br><br>\nUnfortunately I think I lost all my excitement for the wedding.  I am having a hard time keeping track of different resorts and pricing and am getting depressed by the thought of my wedding, which, of course makes me sadder! AH!<br><br>\nWe want to have it on the beach.  Mexico-Mayan Riviera (would like to see ruins) or Hawaii.  About 20-30 people.  Beautiful?  Easiest?  Affordable?  Am I crazy? I need some help.  I would like the wedding ceremony\/reception\/my parents flights\/ my parents hotel stay all for under $10,000.  Is that possible????  <br><br>\nAny responses would be appreciated.  We haven't set a date, waiting to find the resort!<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nHello!<br>\nI'm marrying at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya and my wedding for 46 on the private beach and reception in the private palapa is about $5200. <br><br>\nAfter our booking bonuses with the airline our package for 7 nights (flight\/hotel\/transfers\/tax) for 2 adults and 2 kids was $3100 (was $5100) so with that said I think $10,000 is very doable. <br><br>\nIf you want more info on the resort let me know. Good luck.    <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>43 guests, plus bride and groom \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399399802,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":33,"TotalPages":4,"CurrentPage":20,"NextPage":30,"PreviousPage":10,"LastPage":30},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
